      "writtenOn": "2026-07-27T23:29:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is correct. Requiring users to explicitly enable the option ensures no one can claim the choice was made for them. Enabling GPL licensed code becomes a conscious decision rather than a silent one. This mirrors the approach FFmpeg takes by requiring users to explicitly pass `--enable-gpl`.\n\nAdding a notice whenever GPL licensed code is used is a weaker alternative, since a notice can be ignored just as easily as the note already present in the documentation.",
      "parentUuid": "a672e681_7209b172",
      "revId": "f59b61153bc1cf19542ac65780f3c3a70e465d2a",
      "serverId": "cdcfcfbe-2044-3b1f-b5d4-da77ad542329"
